From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: mediatek: update MT6878 planes at frame end

MT6878 bypasses OVL shadow registers and uses the CPU update path. Updating
plane registers and completing page flips at OVL frame start can therefore
change the buffer while scanout is reading it. The initial frame-start IRQ
was selected while the downstream route was stalled, when completion never
arrived. With the corrected route, OVL completion is available.

A bounded live test changed only OVL0 INTEN from bit 14 to bit 1 while a DRM
sequence event held the vblank reference. The route stayed unchanged, DSC
frames completed without new abnormal EOF, and the user confirmed that
redraw flicker and artifacts disappeared. The event was delivered and USB
SSH remained available. This does not claim accelerated compositor rendering.

Use the ordinary frame-completion vblank source for MT6878 as well. Keep the
setting in SoC data so it survives vblank enable/disable and modesets.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_ovl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_ovl.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_ovl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_ovl.c
@@ -768,7 +768,8 @@ static const struct mtk_disp_ovl_data mt6878_ovl_2l_driver_data = {
 	.formats = mt8173_formats,
 	.num_formats = ARRAY_SIZE(mt8173_formats),
-	.vblank_irq_mask = OVL_FME_START_INT,
+	/* CPU plane updates must not race the frame being fetched. */
+	.vblank_irq_mask = OVL_FME_CPL_INT,
 	.bypass_shadow = true,
 	.reset_on_start = true,
 	.force_relay = true,
 };
